course: dictionary
lesson: 10671
title: Euphemisms: the words we don't say out loud
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things feel too embarrassing or rude to name, so people choose a gentler word instead. A word that is too rude, shocking or embarrassing to say is unmentionable. «Unmentionables» is a funny, polite word for underwear, so the speaker never has to say the plain word.
explain: Context helps you work out the meaning. In «He forgot to pack his unmentionables», the packing makes it clear he forgot his underwear. Ask yourself: what would the sentence say if the author used the plain word? Then check that your meaning fits.
explain: Unmentionable can also describe a subject people would rather not discuss. The clue is in the word itself: un- means not, and mention means to say or name something. So an unmentionable subject is one that is not comfortable to talk about out loud.
fact: Unmentionable means too rude, shocking, embarrassing or upsetting to talk about.
fact: A euphemism is a gentle or polite word used instead of a plain word that might embarrass people.
fact: «Unmentionables» is a humorous word for underwear.
fact: «Body odour» is a polite name for a sweaty smell, and «halitosis» is a polite name for bad breath.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unmentionable means not able to be named out loud.
exercise: In the joke «He forgot to pack his unmentionables», what are his unmentionables? | A tent and a torch | His football boots | His favourite book | *Underwear
exercise: What does unmentionable mean? | Full of bright light | Very long and boring | *Too rude, shocking or embarrassing to talk about | Easy to spell and say
exercise: «Body odour» is a polite name for what? | *A sweaty smell | A sunburn | A loud sneeze | Bad breath
test: Why do people use a word like «unmentionables» instead of the plain word? | *To avoid saying something embarrassing | To describe a sunny day | To show they are cross | To make a sentence longer for a test
test: Which word is the polite name for bad breath? | Glum | Ancient | *Halitosis | Unmentionable
exam: Which word is a humorous, polite name for underwear? | Curt | Glum | *Unmentionables | Barely
